ility carrying its own psionics block. The player picks the variant and the ability separately and they must match; nothing ties the two together. Male: Empathic Transmission (limited to Confusion, Fear, Love/Peacefulness - the limit is ability text), Psionic Invisibility, Alter Aura, Deaden Senses; Radiate Horror Factor at 2, Intuitive Combat at 4, Psychic Omni-Sight at 8. Female: Sense Dimensional Anomaly, Sense Time, See Aura, Psychic Diagnosis, Psychic Purification, Psychic Surgery, two Healing of choice; one more Healing at 3, 6, 9 and 12, Bio-Regenerate (self) at 5 stored as the catalog''s Bio-Regeneration (Super), one Sensitive of choice at 8. || NOT PRINTED: the block gives NO I.S.P. figure and NO psionic tier (minor, major or master) for the Sasquatch, on printed 165 or in the Sasquatch Psionics pages after it; neither is stored. || COMBAT: two actions/attacks per melee at level one is attacks_base 2, +1 at levels 2, 4, 7, 10 and 13. +3 initiative, +3 disarm, +5 pull punch, +1 parry, +2 roll stored. The +1 to automatic dodge is printed at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 14 and stored there; nothing is given at level one. Saves from the Natural Abilities line: +2 vs disease and toxins, +2 vs possession and mind control. || ATTRIBUTES: the roll-an-extra-die-on-a-maximum rule is natural ability text. P.S. and P.E. are supernatural. || O.C.C.s: the book prints Available O.C.C.s: None and then prints the Worldly Sasquatch O.C.C.; occ_restrictions only worldly-sasquatch. The Worldly entry''s all-usual-skills-at-minus-5% is recorded on that class. || NOT STORED: the Human or D-Bee Foundling rules (a child raised by Sasquatch has the same skills +1D4+1 from Wilderness and/or Physical, speaks at about 30%, has its own race''s abilities and not the Sasquatch''s; one who later joins the world adds one language, probably English at +15%, two piloting skills, two W.P. and 1D4 Domestic and/or Technical skills) are GM Notes; a foundling is another race and not this class. Size 7-8 feet, weight 250-400 lb, life span 50 years, average NPC level 1D4+3, allies, enemies and habitat are GM Notes. Standard Equipment is nothing but a feather and perhaps a small sack or pouch, and Money is none; no equipment or money is stored."
---

## Lore

Sasquatch, Big Foot, the Mammoth, the Old Man of the Woods: the names all
belong to one shy, fur-covered giant that most people take for a D-Bee or
a forest spirit. It is neither. The Sasquatch are distant Stone Age
cousins of humanity who walked out of Asia over the Bering land bridge
long ago and settled the forests of the Rocky Mountains. They outlasted
modern man by staying hidden, and the Cataclysm barely touched their
remote ranges. The return of magic did change them: once ordinary flesh,
they are now minor Mega-Damage beings, and their numbers have grown from
a thousand or two to more than ten thousand.

They live as nomads in single families of two to ten, without tribes,
fire, shelter, tools, weapons or clothes. They eat roots, bark, berries,
mushrooms and fruit, take fish and crayfish by hand, and love honey and
maple syrup. They do not hunt. A Sasquatch answers a threat by avoiding
it, hiding from it or walking away, and insults mean nothing to one. When
forced to fight it does only enough to end the danger and escape.

For all their shyness they are curious and kind. They watch travelers from
the trees, steer children away from danger, lead the lost back to camp and
have been known to adopt an orphan. Among themselves they speak with
whistles, grunts, gestures and a private telepathy, and every one of them
is psychic: the males in ways that help them vanish, the females as
healers.

## GM Notes

The book heads the race an NPC and optional player character.

Pick the male or female variant, then the psionics ability of the same
sex. The book prints no I.S.P. and no psionic tier for the Sasquatch; the
G.M. sets both.

A Sasquatch family mates for life and a mated adult will not leave its
family, so an adventuring Sasquatch is an unattached youngster of 15-25 or
a widowed elder. See the Worldly Sasquatch O.C.C.

Human or D-Bee foundling: a child raised by Sasquatch has the same skills
and basic knowledge, plus 1D4+1 skills from Wilderness and/or Physical,
speaks little or no language (about 30%), and uses no weapons, tools or
armor, though it probably wears skins or a poncho. It has its own race''s
natural and psionic abilities and not the Sasquatch''s. A foundling who
later joins the world can add one language of choice (probably English at
+15%), two piloting skills, two W.P.s and 1D4 skills from Domestic and/or
Technical.

Size 7-8 feet (2.1 to 2.4 m). Weight 250 to 400 pounds (112.5 to 180 kg).
Average life span 50 years. NPCs average level 1D4+3.

Equipment: nothing but a feather worn in the hair and perhaps a small sack
or pouch for food and odds and ends. They like combs, pocket mirrors,
honey, jam, candy, sacks, purses and pouches, and leave food or water in
trade for what they take. Money: none.

Allies: other Sasquatch and the Spirit Sasquatch; now and then an Indian
Shaman, a Druid, a psychic or a kind adventurer. Enemies: none as such,
but every stranger is a possible one, and they fear and avoid supernatural
beings. Habitat: the forests of the Canadian Rockies in British Columbia
and Alberta and the deep woods of Washington, Oregon and Montana; fewer in
the Yukon, Idaho, Wyoming, Northern California and Colorado.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'true-sasquatch');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'true-sasquatch';

